# Finance Backend API (Django REST Framework)

## 🚀 Overview

This project is a backend system for managing financial records with role-based access and JWT authentication.

---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

* Django
* Django REST Framework
* JWT Authentication (SimpleJWT)
* SQLite

---

## 📦 Setup Instructions

### 1. Clone Project

```bash
git clone <your-repo-link>
cd finance_project
```

### 2. Create Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate   # Windows
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Run Migrations

```bash
python manage.py migrate
```

### 5. Create Superuser

```bash
python manage.py createsuperuser
```

### 6. Run Server

```bash
python manage.py runserver
```

---

## 🔐 Authentication (JWT)

### Get Token

POST:

```
/api/token/
```

Body:

```json
{
  "username": "your_username",
  "password": "your_password"
}
```

---

### Use Token

Add header:

```
Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
```

---

## 📊 API Endpoints

### Records

| Method | Endpoint           | Description   |
| ------ | ------------------ | ------------- |
| GET    | /api/records/      | List records  |
| POST   | /api/records/      | Create record |
| PUT    | /api/records/<id>/ | Update        |
| DELETE | /api/records/<id>/ | Delete        |

---

## 🧪 Sample Record Input

```json
{
  "amount": 500,
  "type": "expense",
  "category": "Food",
  "date": "2026-04-06",
  "notes": "Lunch"
}
```

---

## 📄 Pagination

* Default page size: 5
* Use:

```
/api/records/?page=2
```

---

## ✅ Features Implemented

* CRUD operations for financial records
* JWT Authentication
* Pagination support
* Input validation
* Admin panel for user management

---

## 📌 Notes

* SQLite used for simplicity
* Roles handled via UserProfile model
* Only authenticated users can access APIs

---
